==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
A borrowing from an {{unk|la|title=unknown}}, possibly {{der|la|ine-ana}} source, cf. Hesychian {{cog|grc|κάπια|t=onions}}<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|page=108|head=cēpa}}</ref> claimed for {{w|Ceryneia}} and the complex of {{cog|ar|قُبَّعَة|t=bulbous hat}}. Given the borrowing of {{cog|sla-pro|*lukъ|t=onion}}, it is probable that the Italians at the date of their expansion also only knew [[ramsons]], as a kind of [[alium#Latin|ālium]]. At least it is known that [[spring onion]] was only introduced in the modern period from China, while [[w:Onion#History|the bulb onion is also Asiatic]], such that ancient Africa knew the cultivated onion only in the north, by generic names like {{cog|egy|ḥḏw}}, it having expanded beyond the Great Desert only by the Arabs under their name {{m|ar|بَصَل}}.

